      "body": "## Overview\r\nFixed  #60752\r\n\r\nThis PR restricts the `is_multi_group` dispatch condition in `invokeNoAuxTc` (csrc/libtorch_stable/moe/grouped_topk_kernels.cu) so configurations with more than 8 expert groups (`n_group > 8`) fall back to the general `grouped_topk_fused_kernel` instead of dispatching to the 8-warp `grouped_topk_fused_small_expert_count_kernel`.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- **Correctness for >8 groups**: Configurations with 9, 16, and 32 groups now produce correct routing indices matching the reference implementation.\r\n- **Safety**: Eliminates out-of-bounds shared memory accesses in `grouped_topk_fused_small_expert_count_kernel`.\r\n- **Zero regression**: Configurations with $\\le 8$ groups (such as standard DeepSeek-style MoE) continue using the optimized small expert count kernel without any behavior or performance changes.\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n### Test Suite Coverage\r\nExtended `tests/kernels/moe/test_grouped_topk.py` to parameterize group counts above 8:\r\n- `(n_expert=144, topk=8, num_expert_group=9, topk_group=4)` (the minimal reproducer from #60752)\r\n- `(n_expert=256, topk=8, num_expert_group=16, topk_group=4)`\r\n- `(n_expert=256, topk=8, num_expert_group=32, topk_group=4)`\r\nAll test cases assert that the kernel output exactly matches the reference PyTorch implementation (`baseline_topk_weights` and `baseline_topk_ids`).\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nThe optimized `grouped_topk_fused_small_expert_count_kernel` is statically bounded for small expert counts, launching with `NumDeepseekExperts` (256 threads / 8 warps) where each warp scores one expert group:\r\n1. The shared memory array `smemGroupScores` has fixed capacity `NumWarps = MaxNumExperts / WARP_SIZE = 256 / 32 = 8`.\r\n2. When `n_group > 8` (e.g., 9, 16, or 32 groups), groups 8 and above are never scored by the warps, causing incorrect expert selection.\r\n3. Furthermore, when `warp 0` reads `smemGroupScores[laneIdx]` in the final selection stage, lanes with `8 <= laneIdx < numGroup` perform out-of-bounds shared memory reads.\r\nPreviously, `is_multi_group` checked `n_group > 1 && num_experts <= NumDeepseekExperts` but did not enforce an upper bound on `n_group`. Adding `(n_group <= NumDeepseekExperts / WARP_SIZE)` routes configurations with `n_group > 8` cleanly to the general fallback kernel `grouped_topk_fused_kernel`, which dynamically sizes block dimensions and shared memory based on `n_group`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**AI assistance was used in this pull request (Gemini code assist)**\r\n",
